    17	
    18	# LangGraph deep-agents skill catalog pattern
    19	
    20	## Insight
    21	LangGraph's deep-agents framework formalizes "skills" as a first-class concept: domain knowledge lives outside the prompt and is loaded only when a task requires it. The system prompt includes a structured **list of available skills containing name, description, tags, and supporting file names** — small enough to include in every request — and the agent pulls in detailed instructions only when needed. This is the pattern the planned skill-loading matrix is reaching for in reverse: gobbi already has per-skill SKILL.md files at the leaves; what is missing is the structured catalog at the top that names exactly which skills each (role, phase) needs.
    22	
    23	## Why it applies
    24	The planned role × phase skill matrix needs a shape. The LangGraph skill-catalog pattern provides one validated answer — a structured catalog (matrix) listing each skill with name + description + tags + file names. Adapted to gobbi: a role × phase table where each cell lists the canonical skill files. The deeper architectural takeaway is that the framework treats this catalog as *part of the system prompt* — i.e., it is something every agent sees on every request. In gobbi terms, this maps to the Load Directives block — the catalog *is* the Load Directives content. The matrix and the Load Directives block are two views of the same data; the validator's job is to keep them in sync.
    25	
    26	## Source
    27	- https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/deepagents/skills
    28	- https://pessini.medium.com/stop-stuffing-your-system-prompt-build-scalable-agent-skills-in-langgraph-a9856378e8f6
    29	- Both accessed 2026-05-23
    30	
    31	## Excerpt
    32	> "LangGraph supports a skills system where domain knowledge lives outside the prompt and is loaded only when a task requires it, allowing agents to see a lightweight catalog first and pull in detailed instructions only when needed."
    33	
