.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/preparation/rawdata/transcript-iter1.jsonl:25:{"parentUuid":"dc3c1535-f824-4056-aae1-93f96a0cd5c5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"732c872b-db1f-4b91-9a6b-c5283b4715f3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VPH5bPPE4mijFTU3efeQTi","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS\nARTIFACT: /playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/preparation/rawdata/sub-steps-a-d-iter1.md\n\n**Summary**: 9 gaps consolidated (Sub-steps B + C). Resolution proposals: 2 `generate-now` (D-3 Planning-brief annotation for adjacent mistakes + D-4 tiny staging design file listing the 5 phase docs), 3 `defer` to backlog (D-2 hooks-domain mistakes, D-6 lifecycle design doc, D-7 hook-authoring skill — N=1 defer until T3 ships), 4 `skip` (D-1 feature dir, D-5 scripts dir, D-8 session-architecture skill, D-9 shell-script-conventions skill). 0 `re-Ideate`.\n\n**Specific items check 8/8 verified**: 6 PRESENT (#1 AI-Provenance-Record trailer, #2 session.template.json [at non-canonical path — see concern], #3 session-start.sh, #4 settings.json hooks block, #5 flock util-linux 2.39.3, #8 preparation/SKILL.md narrow exception), 2 ABSENT as expected (#6 .gobbi/project.json — already backlogged; #7 .claude/scripts/ — executor mkdir).\n\n**Adversarial scan**: 0 overlapping feature work (Bundle A explicitly deferred T1+T3 to this session — confirmed via `notes/2026-05-23-orch-workflow-improvements.md`). 3 mistakes flagged as critical Planning-brief inputs for T1 execution. 1 rule (`stub-redirect-format.md`) has low-to-medium relevance if T1/T3 supersede any existing narrative.\n\n**Concerns flagged**:\n\n1. **Brief imprecision (Specific items #2)**: The delegation brief assumed `session.template.json` lives at `.claude/templates/session.template.json` — that path does not exist. Actual canonical: `.claude/skills/orchestration/templates/session.template.json` (with project mirror at `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/templates/session.template.json`). The file IS present with the correct 14-field manager skeleton matching D-3-4 extraction targets. This is non-blocking but the manager should correct downstream Planning briefs to cite the canonical path. The \"mirror awareness\" question (workspace-only edit vs both) needs surfacing to Planning.\n\n2. **Iron Law 7 procedural reminder is essential for Planning** (per `manager-iter2-brief-failed-iron-law-7-verbatim-spec-recheck.md` — high-severity project mistake from a prior session same week). The 553-line Ideation rawdata is too large for memory-only brief construction; manager must Read freshly when authoring any \"verbatim\" Planning task instruction.\n\n3. **Mirror propagation policy is undefined**: The project has a workspace skill tree at `.claude/skills/` and a project mirror at `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/`. For the session.template.json change and for any orchestration/SKILL.md / git/SKILL.md edits in T1, Planning needs an explicit decision on whether edits propagate to both or only the workspace canonical. Not blocking Preparation, but Planning should AskUserQuestion early.\n\n5 AskUserQuestion cards drafted at the end of the artifact (Cards 1-9 grouped — 5 distinct questions, with the 4 `skip` decisions batched into Card 6). Manager owns presentation."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aa9642df0f15be425 (use SendMessage with to: 'aa9642df0f15be425' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 108285\ntool_uses: 22\nduration_ms: 246901</usage>"}]}]},"uuid":"f009534e-7826-49cb-b585-c6edf8833b80","timestamp":"2026-05-23T18:15:16.696Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are a leader (Principal Investigator / Project Manager) for the gobbi workflow.\n\nYour phase: preparation\nYour iteration: 1\nYour sub-steps: A (Read Ideation) → B (Design + Memory check) → C (Execution Skills check) → D (Gap Resolution Plan), all in one pass.\n\n## Task Description\n\nPreparation Loop runs between Ideation and Planning. Its job: verify project memory + workspace skills are READY for the bundle's Planning + Execution. Surface any gap and propose a resolution per gap. The bundle is `session-foundations-bundle-b` (T1 worktree-first + T3 PostToolUseFailure hook + reconstructor; T2 deferred). Canonical Ideation artifact at `sessions/.../ideation/artifacts/bundle-b-ideation-pass.md` (just produced).\n\n**Sub-step A — Read Ideation Output**\n- Read the canonical Ideation artifact in full.\n- Read `sessions/.../ideation/staging/` to know what's queued for Wrap-up promotion (11 design + 17 discussions + 8 checklists + 9 decisions + 2 scenarios + 12 references + 9 backlogs).\n- Identify all downstream-relevant signals (files / skills / agents / hooks / settings.json / docs that Planning + Execution will touch). Output: a readiness signal list.\n\n**Sub-step B — Design + Memory Readiness Check**\n- For each readiness signal from Sub-step A, scan `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/`, `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/design/`, `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/`, `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/notes/`, `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/decisions/`.\n- Identify missing artifacts that Planning would need (e.g., design constraints not yet recorded, missing mistakes from related work).\n- Propose resolution per missing item: (a) generate-now, (b) defer to backlog, (c) re-Ideate, (d) skip.\n\n**Sub-step C — Execution Skills Readiness Check**\n- T1 + T3 both touch: hook scripts (`.claude/hooks/`), `.claude/settings.json`, agent specs (`.claude/agents/`), workflow skills (`.claude/skills/orchestration/`, `delegation/`, `git/`, `preparation/`, etc.), new shell scripts (`.claude/scripts/`).\n- Identify any missing project-specific skill needed for Execution to operate confidently. Candidates to consider (NOT a requirement to generate any):\n  - A \"hook-authoring\" project skill that crystallizes the bash+jq+strict-mode+guards pattern from `session-start.sh` + the new `post-tool-use-agents.sh`?\n  - A \"session-architecture\" project skill that crystallizes the T1 worktree-first + session-dir-in-worktree pattern for future reference?\n  - A \"shell-script-conventions\" project skill (covering `.claude/scripts/` patterns)?\n  - Or: the existing skills are sufficient because Execution agents load `git/SKILL.md` + `codex/SKILL.md` + `delegation/SKILL.md` per the implicit role × phase matrix.\n- Per `preparation/SKILL.md` § Core Principles: skills are generated NOW only if Planning + Execution NEED them in-session. Speculative skill generation is forbidden.\n- Recommend (a) generate-now, (b) defer to backlog, (c) skip (not needed).\n\n**Sub-step D — Gap Resolution Plan**\n- Consolidate Sub-step B + C gaps into a single resolution table.\n- For each gap: category (design/memory/skill) | severity (Critical / High / Medium / Low) | proposal (generate-now / defer / re-Ideate / skip) | rationale.\n- Surface to manager (via your final report) — manager runs AskUserQuestion per gap.\n\n### Specific Things to Check\n\nGiven the bundle's surface area, verify these specific items are PRESENT (or note their absence):\n\n1. **`git/conventions.md` AI-Provenance-Record trailer scheme** — needed by T1 D-3. Already verified line 118 by iter2+iter3 leaders. Confirm still extant.\n2. **`session.template.json` agents[] schema** — needed by T3 hook design. Already verified by iter1 Sub-step C. Confirm still extant.\n3. **`session-start.sh` as bash+jq precedent** — needed for T3 hook authoring stack. Confirm extant.\n4. **`.claude/settings.json` hooks block** — needed for T3 hook registration. Confirm extant.\n5. **`flock` availability on the build system** — needed for T3 D-3-5 serialization. Test `which flock` empirically.\n6. **`.gobbi/project.json`** — confirmed ABSENT by iter3 Fix C (already staged as backlog).\n7. **`.claude/scripts/` directory existence** — needed for T3 reconstructor. May need to create at Execution start.\n8. **`preparation/SKILL.md` narrow-exception text** — T1 will edit it. Confirm extant.\n\nFor each, report PRESENT / ABSENT (with path verification via `ls -la`).\n\n### Adversarial-mode Scan\n\nPer the Coverage Ownership Matrix + Karpathy 4 modes, also scan for:\n- Any prior \"session-architecture\" feature work in `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/features/` (overlap detection).\n- Any mistakes in `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/` whose domain is `hooks` / `workflow` / `session-mechanics` that should be flagged for Execution awareness.\n- Any rule in `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/rules/` that constrains the bundle's design.\n\n## Context\n\nIdeation Loop closed PASS at iter3. Canonical artifact ready. Now Preparation verifies readiness before Planning decomposes the bundle into ordered Execution tasks.\n\nBundle scope (locked):\n- T1 worktree-first session architecture (with NEW promote-now commit-on-branch absorbed) — touches CLAUDE.md, gobbi/SKILL.md, orchestration/SKILL.md (row 5.5 + agents[] subsection), git/SKILL.md (qualified rule), preparation/SKILL.md (narrow exception extension), 5 loop docs (per-iteration commit cadence)\n- T3 PostToolUse hook + reconstructor — creates `.claude/hooks/post-tool-use-agents.sh` + `.claude/scripts/reconstruct-agents.sh` + edits `.claude/settings.json` + `orchestration/SKILL.md` agents[] subsection + `delegation/SKILL.md` structured-header convention. Backlog: `.gobbi/project.json` bootstrap + schema-extension-agents-status-field.\n- T2 deferred.\n\n## Load Directives\n\n1. Principles: `principles` (mandatory)\n2. Rules: `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/rules/`\n3. Skills:\n   - `mistake` skill (mandatory)\n   - `orchestration/workflow/preparation.md` (phase doc — sub-step orchestration)\n   - `preparation/SKILL.md` (domain — sub-step procedures)\n4. Mistakes:\n   - All 7 (read each at Sub-step B for memory-readiness scan)\n\n## Inputs (FRESH READ)\n\n1. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions