ntent) ✓\n\ntest -L .claude/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md → SYMLINK INTACT ✓\n\nls -la .claude/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md\n→ lrwxrwxrwx ... -> ../../../.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md ✓\n\ngit log --oneline -1 → 14da700 feat(orchestration): add Configuration Step 1 row 5.5 worktree creation ✓\n\ngit show --stat HEAD → 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-) ✓\n```\n\nManual check: Step 1 table rows in order: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5 → 5.5 → 6 → 7 confirmed at lines 98–105.\n\nRow 6 old text \"leave `git.branch`/`git.worktreePath` as `null` until `git` creates the worktree\" — replaced with \"stamp `git.branch` and `git.worktreePath` from the worktree just created in row 5.5\".\n\n**Note for manager**: The Claude Code `Edit` tool refuses to write through symlinks in this environment (error: \"Refusing to write through symlink\"). The edit was performed via the canonical mirror path (`.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md` within the worktree) per the bulk-rewrite fallback in the edit contract. The symlink remained intact — `test -L` confirmed. The Preparation edit contract's post-edit gate passed. This is a discovery worth noting — the edit contract's primary path (`Edit` tool via `.claude/skills/...`) is not available in this executor context; the fallback (canonical mirror path) is the actual working method."}],"totalDurationMs":207394,"totalTokens":110730,"totalToolUseCount":31,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1355,"cache_read_input_tokens":108679,"output_tokens":695,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1355},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":695,"cache_read_input_tokens":108679,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1355,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1355,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats"