e-test regex, G-1 scenario, E-2 scenario, F-4 scenario, validation-strategy table row. Grep audit verifies only audit / historical citations retain bare `session/`.\n\n**Fix B — `PostToolUseFailure` verbatim preservation.** WebFetch on `https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks` succeeded (auto-mode network policy did not block). Verbatim quotes preserved in three places:\n- T3-E-5 entry in Research Insights\n- D-3-3 design narrative\n- T3-I-T3.c checklist item\n- Augmented staged reference `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/staging/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md` with a dedicated \"PostToolUseFailure — verbatim verification\" subsection containing both quotes plus the full 31-event enumeration.\n\nVerbatim captured:\n- Lifecycle table: `| PostToolUseFailure | After a tool call fails |`\n- Exit-code-behavior table: `| PostToolUseFailure | No | Shows stderr to Claude (tool already failed) |`\n\nFallback path (collapse to PostToolUse-only) NOT used.\n\n**Fix C — `.gobbi/project.json` dormant precondition flag.** Empirical `ls -la /playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/project.json` returns \"No such file or directory\" (verified 2026-05-23). Added dormant-precondition note to D-3-3-resolver step (i) narrative. Staged new feature-level backlog at `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/staging/backlogs/feature/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md` describing two pickup paths (in-Execution write or defer). Added T3-I-T3.h checklist item. Updated Scope Contract Out-of-Scope and Backlog promotion log (now nine entries: 8 prior + 1 iter3).\n\n**Scope discipline maintained**: no changes outside the 3 fixes. Sub-step A/B/C content, Framed Problem, all unaffected scenarios, all unaffected design decisions (D-2, D-3, D-4, D-5, D-3-1, D-3-2, D-3-4, D-3-5, D-3-6), and all unaffected checklist items carried forward verbatim from draft-iter2.md.\n\n**Artifacts produced/updated**:\n- `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/draft-iter3.md` (NEW)\n- `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/staging/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md` (UPDATED — Fix B verbatim grounding)\n- `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/staging/backlogs/feature/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md` (NEW — Fix C backlog)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a9980309b0178c9a2 (use SendMessage with to: 'a9980309b0178c9a2' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 140029\ntool_uses: 15\nduration_ms: 577739</usage>"}]}]},"uuid":"f1f25bf3-afd0-4420-975b-1abf417a80c3","timestamp":"2026-05-23T17:27:22.145Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are a leader (Principal Investigator / Project Manager) for the gobbi workflow.\n\nYour phase: ideation\nYour iteration: 3 (FAIL re-entry from iter2; FINAL iter — maxIterations=3)\nYour sub-step: combined Sub-step D revision + WORK (same shape as iter2)\n\n## Task Description\n\niter2 closed FAIL (Claude FAIL + Codex REVISE → pessimistic-union FAIL). The user authorized a SURGICAL 3-fix iter3. SCOPE IS NARROW. Do NOT reopen any decisions beyond the 3 fixes below. Do NOT rewrite sections unrelated to the fixes. Do NOT introduce new design decisions beyond what these fixes require.\n\nPer `mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md` — the iter2 leader fixed F-2 (trailer citation) by reading `git/conventions.md:118` but did NOT whole-file scan `git/conventions.md` when picking F-4's branch name. iter2 introduced a Critical regression on the SAME file. YOU MUST WHOLE-FILE SCAN `git/conventions.md` for any reference you make to it. Per `mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md` — whole-file, not Step-4-only.\n\n### The 3 fixes\n\n**Fix A — F-4 branch prefix regression (user-locked)**\n\nUSER LOCKED via AskUserQuestion: replace `session/{date}-{ssid-short}` with `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}` everywhere it appears in `draft-iter2.md`. `chore` is in the `git/conventions.md:22` registry. The `session-{date}-{ssid-short}` portion becomes the second component (after `chore/`).\n\nBefore writing, WHOLE-FILE READ `git/conventions.md` to confirm:\n- `chore` IS in the type registry at line 22 (verify via Read, do not paraphrase)\n- The second component (after the `/`) has a regex/length constraint you must satisfy (e.g., does `chore/session-2026-05-23-1b26cf20` fit the second-component pattern?)\n- Any branch-name-overall-length constraint (Git limits to 244 chars typically)\n\nFind every occurrence of `session/{date}-{ssid-short}` OR `session/{...}` in draft-iter2.md (`grep -n \"session/\" draft-iter2.md`) and replace each with the new form. Update D-1, T1-I-T1.a, the affected scenarios (G-1, E-2, F-4), and the iter2 Decisions Log line for F-4. Do NOT leave any old form except in audit/fix-decision citations clearly marked as historical.\n\n**Fix B — F-3 PostToolUseFailure verbatim preservation**\n\niter2 claimed WebFetch confirmed `PostToolUseFailure` is documented but provided no verbatim quote. Claude iter2 evaluator's independent WebFetch was blocked by auto-mode network policy.\n\nDo TWO things:\n1. WebFetch `https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks` (and any related Claude Code hooks doc URLs). Extract the VERBATIM passage that mentions `PostToolUseFailure`. If WebFetch is blocked or returns no such passage, follow path 2.\n2. If WebFetch confirms event exists: paste the verbatim quote (with URL + accessed date) into draft-iter3.md's Research Insights section as the T3-E-5 reference body, AND into the D-3-3 design narrative as the citation. Update the staged reference file `sessions/.../ideation/staging/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md` (or create a new one named for the failure event) to include the verbatim quote.\n3. If WebFetch is blocked or event NOT in official docs: change D-3-3 from \"dual registration (PostToolUse + PostToolUseFailure)\" to \"PostToolUse-only with status-via-toolUseResult.status field\" — this collapses to a smaller design but is empirically robust. Document the fallback choice with rationale in iter2/iter3 fix-decisions log.\n\n**Fix C — `.gobbi/project.json` dormant precondition flag**\n\niter2 D-3-3-resolver step (i) reads `$cwd/.gobbi/project.json`. Empirically (verify with `ls -la .gobbi/project.json`) this file DOES NOT EXIST in the repo today. Step (ii) fallback (single-directory scan of `$cwd/.gobbi/projects/`) works currently because exactly one project dir exists, but the dormant precondition is not flagged.\n\nAdd a note to D-3-3-resolver narrative: \"Step (i) `.gobbi/project.json` is a dormant precondition — file does not exist in repo today (verified `ls .gobbi/project.json` returns no-such-file as of 2026-05-23). Resolver currently falls through to step (ii) directory scan, which works while exactly one project dir exists. **Backlog item filed** to add `.gobbi/project.json` as part of Execution (or defer to future session).\"\n\nStage a new feature-level backlog file at `sessions/.../ideation/staging/backlogs/feature/dot-gobbi-project-json-bootstrap.md` using the `backlogs.md` template (per the previous WORK phase pattern; same frontmatter + body shape). Effort: small (single-file write at Execution start). Anchor: D-3-3-resolver step (i) in draft-iter3.md.\n\n### What stays locked (do NOT touch)\n\n- Scope Contract — T1+T3 (T2 deferred)\n- All iter1 + iter2 design decisions that aren't directly affected by the 3 fixes\n- The 7 staged project-level backlogs + 1 staged feature-level backlog from iter1 WORK (you ADD one feature-level backlog for Fix C)\n- 12 staged reference files (you may UPDATE the PostToolUseFailure-related ref per Fix B; do not delete)\n- The 4-stage evaluation procedure\n- Framed Problem, Scenarios outside the F-4 propagation\n- Sub-step A research, Sub-step B Scope Contract, Sub-step C Research Insights (except T3-E-5 update for Fix B)\n\n## Context\n\niter1 REVISE → iter2 FAIL → iter3 surgical 3-fix path approved by user. Budget: iter3 of 3 = LAST iteration. If iter3 also returns REVISE or FAIL, loop aborts (no iter4). User authorized via AskUserQuestion:\n- iter2 escalation path: \"iter3 surgical 3-fix — fix branch prefix + verify PostToolUseFailure + flag project.json\"\n- Branch prefix sub-option: \"(a) chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short} — use existing registry\"\n\n## Load Directives\n\n1. Principles: `principles` (mandatory)\n2. Rules: `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/rules/`\n3. Skills:\n   - `mistake` skill (mandatory)\n   - `orchestration/workflow/ideation.md` (phase doc)\n   - `ideation/SKILL.md` (domain)\n   - `research/SKILL.md` (for Fix B WebFetch)\n4. Mistakes (HIGHEST PRIORITY this iter):\n   - `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md` — iter2 broke on this exact pattern. WHOLE-FILE SCAN git/conventions.md.\n   - `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/manager-iter2-brief-failed-iron-law-7-verbatim-spec-recheck.md` — Read freshly.\n   - `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/claude-evaluator-step4-only-vs-codex-whole-file-grep.md` — Whole-file discipline.\n\n## Inputs\n\n**FRESH READ** (mandatory):\n1. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/draft-iter2.md` — baseline you're revising\n2. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.claude/skills/git/conventions.md` — WHOLE FILE for Fix A\n3. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/evaluation/iter2/claude/*.md` — 8 files for iter2 finding context\n4. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597a