draft + Sub-step A/C/D findings)\n- `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/.../ideation/staging/references/claude-code-posttooluse-hook-schema.md` (update for Fix B)\n\n## Escape Hatch\n\n- If WebFetch (Fix B) is blocked (network policy), use the fallback: collapse to PostToolUse-only. Document with rationale + cite the empirical `toolUseResult.status` field as the status-source. This is OPTION (ii) from iter2's framing.\n- If Fix A whole-file scan reveals a constraint that makes `chore/session-...` invalid (e.g., second-component regex doesn't accept `-`), STOP and emit NEEDS_CONTEXT with the constraint cited verbatim.\n- If you discover the user's locked decision (a) `chore/session-...` is itself non-compliant on whole-file scan, emit NEEDS_CONTEXT immediately — do not invent an alternative.\n\n## Report Format\n\n```\nSTATUS: <DONE|DONE_WITH_CONCERNS|NEEDS_CONTEXT|BLOCKED>\nARTIFACT: /playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/draft-iter3.md\n```\n\nThen body:\n- DONE — draft-iter3.md written; 3 fixes applied; grep audit clean (Fix A); WebFetch outcome documented (Fix B); backlog staged (Fix C).\n- DONE_WITH_CONCERNS — fixes applied; flag specifics (e.g., \"WebFetch blocked; collapsed to PostToolUse-only per fallback\").\n- NEEDS_CONTEXT — paused.\n- BLOCKED — root cause.\n\nNever silently expand scope. Surgical only.","agentId":"a9980309b0178c9a2","agentType":"leader","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Grep audit clean:\n\n- All active design statements (D-1, T1-I-T1.a, T1-I-T1.h, G-1, E-2, F-4, validation-strategy table row) use `chore/session-{date}-{ssid-short}`.\n- Remaining bare `session/` substrings are exclusively:\n  - `gobbi://session/{session-id}/task/...` URI templates (not branch names — the canonical AI-Provenance-Record format; required by `git/conventions.md:118`)\n  - iter3 frontmatter `revision-of-record` describing Fix A\n  - Scope Contract \"T1 branch prefix\" line that ex