dings BEFORE writing the consolidated draft)\n   - `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md` (cite every claim; do not paraphrase from memory)\n\n## Inputs\n\nRead in FULL before authoring any line of the draft:\n\n1. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/sub-step-a-findings-iter1.md` (Framed Problem source)\n2. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/sub-step-c-findings-iter1.md` (Research Insights source)\n3. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/sub-step-d-design-iter1.md` (Scenarios + Implementation Checklist + Design + Validation source)\n\nFor backlog template:\n4. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.claude/skills/memorization/templates/backlogs.md` — exact template to stamp\n\nFor Scope Contract schema:\n5. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.claude/skills/ideation/SKILL.md` § Sub-step B — Lock Scope (the canonical Scope Contract schema reference)\n6. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.claude/skills/evaluation/SKILL.md` § Scope Contract Schema (for any frontmatter field clarifications)\n\n## Constraints / Scope\n\n**In scope**:\n- Write `draft-iter1.md` per required-sections template — 7 sections (Scope Contract → Framed Problem → Research Insights → Scenarios → Implementation Checklist → Design → Decisions Log).\n- Stage 7 project-level + 1 feature-level backlog files per the list above. Use the `backlogs.md` template exactly.\n- Cite every decision in the Decisions Log to the corresponding AskUserQuestion exchange.\n- Cite every research insight to its Sub-step C file:line.\n\n**Out of scope**:\n- New design content. If you discover a gap, STOP and raise NEEDS_CONTEXT.\n- New backlog items not listed above.\n- Stamping reference files (Sub-step C already staged 12 — do not duplicate; the rawdata draft's Research Insights section CITES them by path).\n- Writing to project memory.\n\n**WORK discipline (per ideation/SKILL.md)**:\n- No new content.\n- Cite the discussion (Decisions Log must trace every section's content to a DISCUSSION exchange).\n- Stay terse — the draft is a record of conclusions, not a re-derivation.\n\n## Your Job\n\n1. Load directives top-to-bottom.\n2. Read inputs 1–3 in full (use Read tool — do not Grep).\n3. Read template + schema (inputs 4–6).\n4. Author `draft-iter1.md` with all 7 required sections populated. Aim for 250–400 lines (Sub-step A/C/D combined are ~1100 lines; the canonical draft is a compression, not a re-derivation).\n5. Stamp 8 backlog files (7 project + 1 feature) per the list above.\n6. Verify the WORK exit checklist from `ideation/SKILL.md` § WORK Phase Exit Checklist:\n   - [ ] Rawdata draft has all 7 required sections populated, no `TODO` / `TBD` / `<...>` placeholders\n   - [ ] Every Sub-step C external insight has a corresponding staged reference (already done; verify the count = 12 from Sub-step C)\n   - [ ] Every Sub-step B deferred decision has a backlog entry at the correct level (the 7 project + 1 feature you'll stage)\n   - [ ] Decisions Log cites every AskUserQuestion outcome\n   - [ ] No content beyond what was approved in DISCUSSION\n7. Cite every codebase claim with `file:line`. Cite every research insight with its Sub-step C anchor (e.g., `T1-I-1`).\n\n## Reference Materials\n\n- All inputs listed above\n- The 12 staged reference files at `sessions/.../ideation/staging/references/` (LIST them in the Research Insights section by slug — do not re-read them)\n\n## Escape Hatch\n\nIf you find a gap in the locked decisions (an unanswered question that surfaces while integrating), STOP and raise NEEDS_CONTEXT. Do not invent answers. The user-locked DISCUSSION outputs are the authority.\n\nIf a Sub-step C insight you need to cite contradicts a Sub-step D design decision, surface the contradiction in DONE_WITH_CONCERNS — Sub-step D's user-confirmed design wins, but the contradiction is evaluator-relevant.\n\n## Report Format (wire format — first lines of your final response)\n\n```\nSTATUS: <DONE|DONE_WITH_CONCERNS|NEEDS_CONTEXT|BLOCKED>\nARTIFACT: <path-to-draft-iter1.md>\n```\n\nThen body:\n- **DONE** — draft written; all 7 sections populated; 8 backlog files staged; exit checklist all-green. One-line summary per section.\n- **DONE_WITH_CONCERNS** — draft + backlogs written; flag specific concerns (e.g., \"Decisions Log line 47 cites an exchange whose AskUserQuestion result I had to infer from context\").\n- **NEEDS_CONTEXT** — gap found; specify what's needed.\n- **BLOCKED** — root cause + evidence.\n\nNever silently produce work you are unsure about — use DONE_WITH_CONCERNS when uncertain.","agentId":"a7c40b29039f13d86","agentType":"leader","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All artifacts staged correctly. WORK exit checklist verification:\n\n- ✅ Rawdata draft has all 7 required sections (Scope Contract, Framed Problem, Research Insights, Scenarios, Implementation Checklist, Design, Decisions Log) — no `TODO` / `TBD` / `<...>` placeholders\n- ✅ 12 staged external reference files present at `staging/references/` (one per Sub-step C external insight: 4 T1 + 4 T2 + 4 T3 = 12)\n- ✅ Every Sub-step B deferred decision has a backlog entry: 7 project + 1 feature = 8 staged backlogs\n- ✅ Decisions Log cites every AskUserQuestion outcome (15 chronological entries) + reference + backlog promotion logs\n- ✅ No new content beyond DISCUSSION-approved decisions\n\n```\nSTATUS: DONE\nARTIFACT: /playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/draft-iter1.md\n```\n\n**Summary by section**\n\n- **Scope Contract** — feature `session-foundations-bundle-b`; In-Scope = T1 (with NEW absorbed) + T3; Out-of-Scope explicitly lists T2 deferral, Codex CI, Item 2-1, chat-mode redesign, alternative collapsing strategies, broader contract-verifier re-framing, template `status` field extension; 11 locked decisions traced to AskUserQuestion outcomes; 5 success criteria; 8 Deferred items pointing to backlog slugs.\n- **Framed Problem** — two independent framings (T1 + T3), each filling root-cause / impact (who-severity-cost) / 4 success criteria / prior attempts / counterfactual+steel-man / re-framing conclusion per the template. Every claim cites a source.\n- **Research Insights** — 5 internal + 4 external insights per task (T1, T3 fully consumed; T2 preserved-but-not-consumed); 12 external insights link to `staging/references/{slug}.md` paths by name.\n- **Scenarios** — T1: 2 golden + 3 edge + 3 failure + adversarial declared-not-applicable. T3: 2 golden + 4 edge + 3 failure + adversarial declared-not-applicable. Each scenario anchored to insight IDs.\n- **Implementation Checklist** — T1: 8 anchored items (T1-I-T1.a through T1-I-T1.h). T3: 6 anchored items (T3-I-T3.a through T3-I-T3.f). Each cites design decisions + insights.\n- **Design** — 5 T1 design decisions (D-1 to D-5) + 4 T3 design decisions (D-3-1 to D-3-4); each with rationale, anchored insights, trade-off considered, validation method; consolidated validation strategy table.\n- **Decisions Log** — 15 chronological AskUserQuestion outcomes split across Sub-step A round 1 (4), Sub-step A round 2 (5), Sub-step B (1), Sub-step C (1), Sub-step D round 1 (2), Sub-step D round 2 (2); plus Reference Promotion Log (12 slugs grouped by task) and Backlog Promotion Log (7 project + 1 feature).\n\n**Staged backlogs** (8 total, all stamped from `backlogs.md` template at `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.claude/skills/memorization/templates/backlogs.md`, with required frontmatter `title / status: deferred / project / feature / task / anchor_session / created / tags / disposition: open` plus Context / Why deferred / When to pick up / Suggested approach / Effort estimate / Originating session / Anchor body):\n\nProject-level (`staging/backlogs/project/`):\n1. `item-1-2-skill-loading-discipline.md`\n2. `codex-ci-integration-for-dual-system-eval.md`\n3. `item-2-1-auto-mode-silence-vs-always-ask.md`\n4. `chat-mode-tiki-taka-redesign.md`\n5. `item-1-3-two-surface-collapsing-strategy.md`\n6. `item-1-3-symlink-into-worktree-alternative.md`\n7. `item-1-2-broader-delegation-contract-verifier.md`\n\nFeature-level (`staging/backlogs/feature/`):\n8. `schema-extension-agents-status-field.md`\n\nAll artifact paths:\n\n- `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/draft-iter1.md`\n- `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/staging/backlogs/project/item-1-2-skill-loading-discipline.md`\n- `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/staging/backlogs/project/codex-ci-integration-for-dual-system-eval.md`\n- `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/staging/backlogs/project/item-2-1-auto-mode-silence-vs-always-ask.md`\n- `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/staging/backlogs/project/chat-mode-tiki-taka-redesign.md`\n- `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/staging/backlogs/project/item-1-3-two-surface-collapsing-strategy.md`\n- `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/staging/backlogs/project/item-1-3-symlink-into-worktree-alternative.md`\n- `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/staging/backlogs/project/item-1-2-broader-delegation-contract-verifier.md`\n- `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gob