aration/promote-now` with canonical `gobbi://session/{session-id}/task/{task-id}` per **freshly re-read `git/conventions.md:118`** (verbatim quoted); `{task-id}` = `preparation-promote-now-iter{n}`. Updated both D-3 narrative and T1-I-T1.d checklist item. Audit grep clean (only intentional fix-decision citations contain the old form).\n- **Finding 3 (P2 / O1 — `PostToolUseFailure`)** — **WebFetched `https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks` 2026-05-23**: `PostToolUseFailure` IS officially documented as a shell-command-supported hook event (one of 31 documented events with explicit decision-control semantics). Outcome (i): KEPT D-3-3 dual registration; ADDED official-doc citation (T3-E-5 inline; D-3-3 narrative; T3-I-T3.c checklist; Scope Contract Decisions Locked).\n- **Finding 4 (COD-PROJ-001 — branch naming)** — Picked **option (c)** session-id-based `session/{date}-{ssid-short}` (not feature-slug-dependent). Rationale: preserves Scope-Contract-locked row 5.5 placement; avoids rename complexity of (b); branch is short-lived so semantic-name cost is bounded. Updated D-1 + T1-I-T1.a + G-1/E-2 scenarios.\n- **Finding 5 (COD-STRUCT-001 — resolver)** — Added D-3-3-resolver. Project-name precedence: **(ii) read `$cwd/.gobbi/project.json`** then **(i) `.gobbi/projects/` directory scan fallback**. Date prefix: **(b) scan `$cwd/.gobbi/projects/<name>/sessions/` for dir ending `-<session_id>`**. Rationale documented (clock-correctness-independent vs option a; not circular vs option c).\n- **Finding 6 (COD-CONS — D-3-4 vs T3-I-3 tension)** — Explicitly disambiguated in D-3-4 narrative + T3-I-3 description: hook stdin has TWO sides; input side (`tool_input.prompt`, `tool_input.model`) supplies `step/phase/iter/model`; result side (`toolUseResult`) supplies output telemetry only. No inconsistency.\n- **Finding 7 (COD-STRUCT-003 — correlation key)** — Added D-3-6: exact jq paths documented (`message.content[].id` for `tool_use` line; `message.content[].tool_use_id` for `tool_result` line). Anchored to empirical reference file line 50.\n\n**Lower-priority** (F-8 + F-9 in Decisions Log): performance bounds documented (`maxIterations × 5 loops = 15 commits + N hook fires`); path-vocabulary reconciliation note CL-1 added; hook stdin field enumeration added in D-3-3-resolver; privacy/retention + DQ-anchor visibility + `recordedBy` field deferred with rationale.\n\n**Scope Contract preserved**: T1 + T3 (T2 deferred) unchanged; user-locked decisions on worktree-first-uniform, session-dir-in-worktree, mechanism (c), dual registration, per-iteration commit cadence, direct mode opt-out all carry forward."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a219e897e6508a1eb (use SendMessage with to: 'a219e897e6508a1eb' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 196672\ntool_uses: 31\nduration_ms: 542921</usage>"}]}]},"uuid":"4fd08d11-3dec-4d4c-94e4-921e4a0eed43","timestamp":"2026-05-23T16:48:35.198Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are a leader (Principal Investigator / Project Manager) for the gobbi workflow.\n\nYour phase: ideation\nYour iteration: 2 (REVISE re-entry from iter1)\nYour sub-step: combined Sub-step D revision + WORK — produce updated draft-iter2.md addressing all evaluator findings, OR re-route to Sub-step C if a finding requires fresh research.\n\n## Task Description\n\niter1 closed with REVISE verdict from BOTH systems (Claude evaluator + Codex evaluator). You must address every High-severity finding listed below and produce an updated rawdata draft at `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/draft-iter2.md`.\n\nPer `mistakes/manager-iter2-brief-failed-iron-law-7-verbatim-spec-recheck.md`: you MUST FRESHLY READ the iter1 draft and the iter1 evaluation files. Do NOT reconstruct from this brief's paraphrasing — this brief lists findings as pointers; you fetch the verbatim from the source files.\n\n### Findings to address (verbatim cites are in the source files; this list is for routing)\n\n**Convergent High (both Claude + Codex agree)**:\n\n1. **R1 / COD-STRUCT-002 — Concurrent PostToolUse hook fires can lose-update `session.json.agents[]`.**\n   - Source: `sessions/.../ideation/evaluation/iter1/claude/risk.md` (R1) + `sessions/.../ideation/evaluation/iter1/codex/structure.md` (COD-STRUCT-002).\n   - Required fix: add a serialization mechanism to the hook design. Three candidates surfaced; you pick one with rationale: (a) POSIX advisory `flock` on `session.json` (bash-compatible, `flock -x <fd>`); (b) per-spawn file pattern (each hook invocation writes to `session.json.d/{agentId}.json`, reconstructor consolidates at Wrap-up); (c) accept lost-update + rely solely on reconstructor for repair. You may surface NEEDS_CONTEXT if you find a fourth option you prefer over these.\n   - Update Sub-step D design: new design decision D-3-5 (serialization mechanism); update D-3-1 hook authoring stack to call out the serialization primitive; update D-3-2 reconstructor algorithm to handle the chosen serialization (e.g., per-spawn files require consolidation).\n   - Validation method: smoke test with two concurrent Task spawns; verify agents[] gains both entries (no lost update).\n\n**Claude-only High**:\n\n2. **P1 / C1 — Invented `AI-Provenance-Record` trailer scheme `gobbi://session/{ssid}/loop/preparation/promote-now` contradicts the canonical schema in `git/conventions.md`.**\n   - Source: `sessions/.../ideation/evaluation/iter1/claude/project.md` (P1) + `sessions/.../ideation/evaluation/iter1/claude/consistency.md` (C1).\n   - The canonical form per `git/conventions.md:118` (verify by Read) is `gobbi://session/{session-id}/task/{task-id}`.\n   - Required fix: replace BOTH occurrences in iter1 draft (D-3 narrative + checklist T1.d) with the canonical form. The `{task-id}` should be the Preparation `generate-now` task identifier (TBD — use the slug or task ID from session.json; clarify in your fix narrative).\n   - Validation method: grep audit `grep -rn \"AI-Provenance-Record\" draft-iter2.md` returns only the canonical form.\n\n3. **P2 / O1 — `PostToolUseFailure` event is only attested in community blog (`claudefa.st`), NOT in the official Claude Code docs cited at T3-E-1.**\n   - Source: `sessions/.../ideation/evaluation/iter1/claude/project.md` (P2) + `sessions/.../ideation/evaluation/iter1/claude/overall.md` (O1).\n   - The D-3-3 dual registration depends on this event being shell-command-supported.\n   - Required fix: VERIFY via WebFetch (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks or the canonical Claude Code hooks docs). Two outcomes:\n     - (i) `PostToolUseFailure` IS in the official docs → keep D-3-3 dual registration; add the official-doc citation to the design.\n     - (ii) `PostToolUseFailure` is NOT in the official docs → drop dual registration; collapse D-3-3 to PostToolUse-only; failed spawns get `status: \"failed\"` recorded via `toolUseResult.status` field (which IS in the empirical transcript per T3-I-2).\n   - The choice is yours based on verification; document the evidence either way.\n\n**Codex-only High**:\n\n4. **COD-PROJ-001 — Row 5.5 worktree creation needs branch naming convention, but task slug isn't known until Sub-step B (post-Configuration).**\n   - Source: `sessions/.../ideation/evaluation/iter1/codex/project.md`.\n   - Required fix: pick one design path:\n     - (a) Defer worktree creation from row 5.5 to Sub-step B end (after Scope Contract lock — task slug known). Update D-1 to specify Sub-step B post-lock as the new creation point.\n     - (b) Use placeholder branch name at row 5.5 (e.g., `session/{date}-{ssid-short}`), rename after Sub-step B via `git branch -m`. Update D-1 with the rename step.\n     - (c) Lock branch naming convention to a session-id-based form that doesn't need task slug (e.g., `session/{ssid-short}`).\n   - Pick (a) unless you find a strong reason to favor (b) or (c). Justify.\n\n5. **COD-STRUCT-001 — Hook session-dir resolver underspecified.**\n   - Source: `sessions/.../ideation/evaluation/iter1/codex/structure.md`.\n   - PostToolUse hook stdin has `session_id` and `cwd` per the official docs. The session dir is at `$cwd/.gobbi/projects/<project-name>/sessions/{date}-{session_id}/session.json`. The hook needs:\n     - `<project-name>` — derived from where? Three options: (i) scan `$cwd/.gobbi/projects/` for the single project dir; (ii) read `$cwd/.gobbi/project.json` for the project pointer (if it exists); (iii) extract from `git -C \"$cwd\" remote get-url origin` (repo-name-as-project-name).\n     - `{date}` prefix — derived from where? Three options: (a) compute `date +%Y-%m-%d` at hook time (may be wrong if session crosses midnight); (b) scan `$cwd/.gobbi/projects/<name>/sessions/` for the dir ending in `-<session_id>` (correct but disk-intensive); (c) read it from `session.json.startedAt` after locating the session by `session_id`.\n   - Required fix: pick one combination with rationale. Recommend (i) project-scan + (b) sessions-scan as the robust default (handles both edge cases). Update D-3 to specify the resolver algorithm.\n\n**Codex-only Medium (also need addressing)**:\n\n6. **COD-CONS — T3-I-3 (step/phase/iter/model NOT in toolUseResult) vs D-3-4 (prompt-header parsing is sufficient) — tension noted but not resolved.**\n   - Source: `sessions/.../ideation/evaluation/iter1/codex/consistency.md`.\n   - This is a misread by Codex IMO — T3-I-3 says these fields aren't in `toolUseResult` (the result side), but D-3-4 correctly notes they ARE in `tool_input.prompt` (the input side) AND `tool_input.model` (the input model field). The tension is between two different sides of the same hook stdin payload — D-3-4 extracts from `tool_input` (correct), T3-I-3 noted `toolUseResult` doesn't have them (correct).\n   - Required fix: explicitly document this in D-3-4 narrative — \"step/phase/iter come from `tool_input.prompt` structured headers; model comes from `tool_input.model`; `toolUseResult` is consulted only for output telemetry (agentId, usage, totalDurationMs, toolStats).\" This resolves the tension by clarifying which side provides which field.\n\n7. **COD-STRUCT-003 — Transcript `tool_use_id` correlation key needs structural contract.**\n   - Source: `sessions/.../ideation/evaluation/iter1/codex/structure.md`.\n   - The hook + reconstructor need to correlate hook's `tool_use_id` (stdin) with transcript `toolUseResult` records. Empirically the transcript line's `message.content[].tool_use_id` (or equivalent) matches; specify the exact jq path used to correlate.\n   - Required fix: document the correlation key in D-3 narrative + reconstructor algorithm spec. Cite the empirical transcript inspection result.\n\n**Lower-priority findings** (per evaluator summaries — investigate during iter2; address or defer with rationale):\n- Performance: per-iteration commit cadence O(n) scaling for long sessions (Codex pf finding). Mitigation: cite that worst case is bounded by maxIterations × 5 loops = 15 commits per session.\n- Aesthetics: minor naming inconsistencies, section heading deviation (Codex aesthetics).\n- Usage: hook stdin field list incomplete for consumer use (Codex usage). Mitigation: expand D-3-1 to enumerate the hook stdin fields used.\n\n### What stays locked (Scope Contract + iter1 user-confirmed decisions)\n\nThese DO NOT change in iter2 — they are user-locked via AskUserQuestion. If a finding asks you to reopen them, surface NEEDS_CONTEXT.\n\n- Feature: `session-foundations-bundle-b`\n- 2 tasks (T1 + T3); T2 deferred\n- T1 worktree-first uniform; session dir lives in worktree (PR absorbs on merge); NEW absorbed as commit-on-branch\n- T3 mechanism (c) hook + reconstructor; hook contract verified for PostToolUse (not PostToolUseFailure — that's finding 3 above)\n- D-3-1 bash+jq stack\n- D-3-2 verify-and-fix reconstructor algorithm\n- D-3-4 hybrid metadata extraction (clarified in finding 6 fix)\n- D-4 per-iteration session-memory commit cadence; chore(session): subject\n- D-5 direct mode retained\n- 7 project + 1 feature backlog items already staged (no changes needed)\n\n## Context\n\niter1 closed REVISE both systems. Findings span design (R1, COD-STRUCT-001, COD-PROJ-001, COD-CONS), mechanical (P1 trailer), and verification gap (P2). User authorized full remediation in iter2.\n\nThis is iter2 of maxIterations=3. If iter2 also returns REVISE, you have iter3 left. iter3 REVISE → loop abort (FAIL escalation).\n\n## Load Directives (in order)\n\n1. Principles:\n   - `principles` skill (mandatory)\n2. Rules:\n   - All files under `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/rules/`\n3. Skills:\n   - `mistake` skill (mandatory)\n   - `orchestration/workflow/ideation.md` (phase doc — Sub-step D + WORK procedure)\n   - `ideation/SKILL.md` (domain)\n   - `research/SKILL.md` (you'll need it for the P2/O1 verification web-fetch)\n4. Mistakes (HIGHEST PRIORITY this iter):\n   - `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/manager-iter2-brief-failed-iron-law-7-verbatim-spec-recheck.md` — YOU MUST FRESHLY READ all iter1 source artifacts. Do NOT reconstruct from this brief.\n   - `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/leader-iter2-verification-claim-without-evidence.md` — Cite every claim freshly; the P1/C1 trailer-citation drift you must FIX is itself an instance of this pattern.\n   - `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md` — for the verification gap (P2/O1).\n\n## Inputs (FRESHLY READ — do not paraphrase from this brief)\n\n**iter1 artifacts** (in order of priority for your re-read):\n1. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/draft-iter1.md` — the iter1 canonical draft; the baseline you revise.\n2. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/sub-step-d-design-iter1.md` — Sub-step D source (most of which holds).\n3. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/evaluation/iter1/claude/*.md` — 8 files; Claude eval findings (P1, P2, R1, C1, O1 you must address).\n4. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/evaluation/iter1/codex/*.md` — 8 files; Codex eval findings (COD-PROJ-001, COD-STRUCT-001/002/003, COD-CONS you must address).\n5. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/sub-step-c-findings-iter1.md` — research context (T3-I-3 in particular for finding 6 disambiguation).\n\n**Spec re-reads** (mandatory — do not reconstruct from memory):\n6. `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.claude/skills/git/conventions.md` — the canonical AI-Provenance-Record trailer form (finding 2/P1/C1 target).\n7. Official Claude Code hooks docs at https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks — for finding 3/P2/O1 PostToolUseFailure verification (use WebFetch).\n\n## Constraints / Scope\n\n**In scope**:\n- Address ALL 7 findings listed above (1-7) with concrete fixes in draft-iter2.md.\n- Update Sub-step D design decisions (add D-3-5 for serialization; update D-1, D-3, D-3-1, D-3-3, D-3-4 as needed).\n- Update Implementation Checklist to reflect new design decisions (e.g., D-3-5 serialization mechanism becomes a new checklist item).\n- Verify P2/O1 via WebFetch (one external research item, scoped narrowly).\n- Cite EVERY claim with file:line — especially the canonical AI-Provenance-Record form from `git/conventions.md`.\n- Update Decisions Log to include iter2 fix-decisions traceable to specific findings.\n\n**Out of scope**:\n- Reopening Scope Contract decisions (T1+T3, T2 deferred, etc.).\n- Stamping new reference files (the 12 from Sub-step C remain valid; you can ADD one if PostToolUseFailure verification produces a new external source).\n- Stamping new backlog files (the 8 remain valid; you can ADD one only if a finding requires a new deferral).\n- Re-doing Sub-step A or B.\n- Editing iter1 artifacts (those are preserved as audit trail).\n\n**WORK discipline**:\n- The draft-iter2.md is the iter2 canonical artifact. It REPLACES draft-iter1.md as the input to iter2's EVALUATION.\n- Use the same 7-section required template (Scope Contract → Framed Problem → Research Insights → Scenarios → Implementation Checklist → Design → Decisions Log).\n- Append to the Decisions Log a new subsection \"iter2 fix-decisions\" listing each finding addressed + the chosen fix + the source of authority (file:line citation).\n\n## Your Job\n\n1. Load directives top-to-bottom.\n2. FRESHLY READ all 5 input artifacts (iter1 draft + Sub-step D + 16 evaluation files + Sub-step C findings). Do not skim.\n3. FRESHLY READ `git/conventions.md` for the canonical trailer form.\n4. WebFetch the Claude Code hooks official docs to verify `PostToolUseFailure` attestation (finding 3). Record the result.\n5. For each finding (1-7), draft the fix with explicit citation. Update Sub-step D design accordingly.\n6. Author `draft-iter2.md` at the path above. Maintain all sections; update Design section + Implementation Checklist + Decisions Log to reflect iter2 changes. The 7 unchanged sections (Scope Contract, Framed Problem, Research Insights, Scenarios) carry forward from iter1 verbatim unless a finding required edits there too.\n7. Verify the WORK exit checklist: no TODO / TBD / <...> placeholders; every section populated; Decisions Log cites every fix-decision; no out-of-scope content.\n\n## Reference Materials\n\n- `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/staging/references/*.md` — 12 staged references (T1 + T3 sources)\n- `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/staging/backlogs/` — 8 backlog items\n- The relevant skill files for cross-checks (git/SKILL.md, preparation/SKILL.md, orchestration/SKILL.md, etc.) — Read fresh, do not paraphrase.\n\n## Escape Hatch\n\n- If WebFetch of the Claude Code hooks docs fails (network / 404), report DONE_WITH_CONCERNS — note that finding 3/P2/O1 must be empirically verified via test-hook in Execution rather than via doc citation.\n- If a finding's required fix forces reopening a Scope Contract decision (e.g., R1 fix requires changing the hook architecture so fundamentally that \"(c) hook + reconstructor\" is no longer accurate), STOP and emit NEEDS_CONTEXT with explicit user-question.\n- If two findings have contradictory fixes (e.g., COD-PROJ-001 fix conflicts with COD-STRUCT-001 fix), surface the contradiction in DONE_WITH_CONCERNS — pick one with rationale, flag the other.\n\n## Report Format (wire format — first lines of your final response)\n\n```\nSTATUS: <DONE|DONE_WITH_CONCERNS|NEEDS_CONTEXT|BLOCKED>\nARTIFACT: /playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/draft-iter2.md\n```\n\nThen body:\n- **DONE** — draft-iter2.md written; all 7 findings addressed; cite which design decisions were updated/added (e.g., \"added D-3-5; updated D-1 + D-3 + D-3-1 + D-3-3 + D-3-4\"); one-line per finding (e.g., \"Finding 1: chose flock(2) on session.json; D-3-5 added with rationale + validation\").\n- **DONE_WITH_CONCERNS** — draft written; flag specific concerns (e.g., \"WebFetch returned 404; PostToolUseFailure not verifiable from official docs; chose to drop dual registration per finding 3 option (ii)\").\n- **NEEDS_CONTEXT** — paused; specific blocker.\n- **BLOCKED** — root cause + evidence.\n\nNever silently produce work you are unsure about. Iron Law 7: cite freshly.","agentId":"a219e897e6508a1eb","agentType":"leader","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All `loop/preparation/promote-now` occurrences are inside intentional audit/fix-decision citations (lines 312 + 488), not in active normative content. The canonical `task/{task-id}` form is used everywhere else.\n\nFinal structural confirmation: 502 lines, 12 H2 sections covering the full 7-section template plus Decisions Log sub-structure. All 7 findings addressed with explicit traceability in the iter2 fix-decisions subsection.\n\n---\n\nSTATUS: DONE\nARTIFACT: /playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/ideation/rawdata/draft-iter2.md\n\n**Design decisions changed**: added D-3-3-resolver, D-3-5, D-3-6; updated D-1, D-3, D-3-1, D-3-2, D-3-3, D-3-4. **Implementation checklist changed**: T1-I-T1.a, T1-I-T1.d updated; T1-I-T1.i, T1-I-T1.j added; T3-I-T3.a, T3-I-T3.b, T3-I-T3.c, T3-I-T3.e updated; T3-I-T3.g added; CL-1 process item added. **Scenarios changed**: G-1, E-2 updated; F-4, E-5, G-3 added. **Research Insights changed**: T3-I-3 narrative clarified (input-side / result-side disambiguation); T3-E-5 added (iter2 official-doc verification of `PostToolUseFailure`).\n\n**One-line per finding**:\n\n- **Finding 1 (R1 / COD-STRUCT-002)** — Chose **POSIX `flock -x` on `session.json`** (option a). Added D-3-5 with rationale: smallest change, preserves bash+jq precedent, serializes both hook + reconstructor; rejected per-spawn-files (b) and accept-lost-update (c) with stated reasons. Validation: concurrent-fire smoke test + `kill -9` lock-release test.\n- **Finding 2 (P1 / C1 — trailer)** — Replaced invented `loop/preparation/promote-now` with canonical `gobbi://session/{session-id}/task/{task-id}` per **freshly re-read `git/conventions.md:118`** (verbatim quoted); `{task-id}` = `preparation-promote-now-iter{n}`. Updated both D-3 narrative and T1-I-T1.d checklist item. Audit grep clean (only intentional fix-decision citations contain the old form).\n- **Finding 3 (P2 / O1 — `PostToolUseFailure`)** — **WebFetched `https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks` 2026-05-23**: `PostToolUseFailure` IS officially documented as a shell-command-supported hook event (one of 31 documented events with explicit decision-control semantics). Outcome (i): KEPT D-3-3 dual registration; ADDED official-doc citation (T3-E-5 inline; D-3-3 narrative; T3-I-T3.c checklist; Scope Contract Decisions Locked).\n- **Finding 4 (COD-PROJ-001 — branch naming)** — Picked **option (c)** session-id-based `session/{date}-{ssid-short}` (not feature-slug-dependent). Rationale: preserves Scope-Contract-locked row 5.5 placement; avoids rename complexity of (b); branch is short-lived so semantic-name cost is bounded. Updated D-1 + T1-I-T1.a + G-1/E-2 scenarios.\n- **Finding 5 (COD-STRUCT-001 — resolver)** — Added D-3-3-resolver. Project-name precedence: **(ii) read `$cwd/.gobbi/project.json`** then **(i) `.gobbi/projects/` directory scan fallback**. Date prefix: **(b) scan `$cwd/.gobbi/projects/<name>/sessions/` for dir ending `-<session_id>`**. Rationale documented (clock-correctness-independent vs option a; not circular vs option c).\n- **Finding 6 (COD-CONS — D-3-4 vs T3-I-3 tension)** — Explicitly disambiguated in D-3-4 narrative + T3-I-3 description: hook stdin has TWO sides; input side (`tool_input.prompt`, `tool_input.model`) supplies `step/phase/iter/model`; result side (`toolUseResult`) supplies output telemetry only. No inconsistency.\n- **Finding 7 (COD-STRUCT-003 — correlation key)** — Added D-3-6: exact jq paths documented (`message.content[].id` for `tool_use` line; `message.content[].tool_use_id` for `tool_result` line). Anchored to empirical reference file line 50.\n\n**Lower-priority** (F-8 + F-9 in Decisions Log): performance bounds documented (`maxIterations × 5 loops = 15 commits + N hook fires`); path-vocabulary reconciliation note CL-1 added; hook stdin field enumeration added in D-3-3-resolver; privacy/retention + DQ-anchor visibility + `recordedBy` field deferred with rationale.\n\n**Scope Contract preserved**: T1 + T3 (T2 deferred) unchanged; user-locked decisions on worktree-first-uniform, session-dir-in-worktree, mechanism (c), dual registration, per