.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-23-1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac/planning/rawdata/transcript-iter1.jsonl:1:{"parentUuid":"b9295dbb-32fe-4bf1-9334-f755bec09512","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XBoS1jEL2waAfptikpKcxL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NXFjA2yBEwDaDUzuYEcK1g","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Planning iter1 — Sub-steps A-D","subagent_type":"leader","model":"opus","prompt":"You are a leader (Principal Investigator / Project Manager) for the gobbi workflow.\n\nPhase: planning\nIteration: 1\nSub-steps: A (Read Ideation Output) → B (File Decomp + Task Def) → C (Dependency Graph) → D (Agent Assignment), all in one pass.\n\n## Task Description\n\nPlanning Loop runs between Preparation and Execution. Its job: decompose the Ideation-locked bundle into ordered, scoped Execution tasks each with file map / scope / verification anchor / agent assignment.\n\n**Bundle**: `session-foundations-bundle-b` (T1 worktree-first session architecture with NEW absorbed + T3 PostToolUseFailure hook + reconstructor; T2 deferred).\n\n**Inputs already locked from upstream**:\n- Ideation iter3 PASS canonical artifact at `sessions/.../ideation/artifacts/bundle-b-ideation-pass.md`\n- Ideation 9-step Planning decomposition recommendation embedded in the artifact\n- Preparation iter3 PASS canonical artifact at `sessions/.../preparation/artifacts/preparation.md`\n- Preparation iter3 mirror policy + symlink-preservation edit contract (locked)\n- Preparation iter3 D-3 mistake-load-directive requirement for T1 task briefs\n- Preparation iter3 D-4 workflow phase doc set (5 files, not 7)\n\n### Sub-step A — Read Ideation + Preparation Output\n\nRead both canonical artifacts in full. Confirm scope is still T1 + T3 (T2 deferred). Enumerate the in-scope implementation checklist items (T1.a-T1.j + T3.a-T3.h per the iter3 design) as task seeds.\n\n### Sub-step B — File Decomposition + Task Definition\n\nRefine Ideation's 9-step decomposition into actual Planning tasks. For each task:\n- Task name + ID (e.g., T1.1, T1.2, T3.1, ...)\n- Scope (which files touched + what type of change)\n- Anchor (which Sub-step D design decision + which Implementation Checklist item this implements)\n- Acceptance criteria (verifiable yes/no per `evaluation/SKILL.md` checklist-item pattern)\n- Estimated effort (Small / Medium / Large — see below for boundaries)\n\nEffort boundaries:\n- Small = ~1 perspective-pair edit, single file\n- Medium = 2-5 files OR one file with substantial body change OR new artifact creation\n- Large = 5+ files OR a new artifact + cross-cutting wire-up\n\nFor this bundle, suggest the following task topology (refine if needed):\n- **T1.1** Edit orchestration/SKILL.md (Configuration Step 1 row 5.5 insertion + row 6 stamp updates + agents[] manager-append narrative → hook-based)\n- **T1.2** Edit git/SKILL.md (Memory Access Matrix qualified rule + Critical rule paragraph + P2 invocation note)\n- **T1.3** Edit preparation/SKILL.md (narrow-exception extension with commit-on-branch + `git -C \"$worktreePath\"` semantics)\n- **T1.4** Edit 5 workflow phase docs (per-iter commit cadence at MEMORIZATION exit — `ideation.md`, `preparation.md`, `planning.md`, `execution.md`, `wrap-up.md`)\n- **T1.5** Edit gobbi/SKILL.md + delegation/SKILL.md (cross-reference + main-tree boilerplate grep audit per T1-I-T1.i)\n- **T1.6** Rollback semantics doc patch (preparation/SKILL.md or git/SKILL.md) per T1-I-T1.j\n- **T3.1** Create `.claude/hooks/post-tool-use-agents.sh` (bash + jq + flock; full implementation per D-3-1/D-3-5/D-3-6)\n- **T3.2** Create `.claude/scripts/reconstruct-agents.sh` (bash + jq; verify-and-fix algorithm per D-3-2; shares jq snippets with T3.1)\n- **T3.3** Edit `.claude/settings.json` (add PostToolUse + PostToolUseFailure hooks blocks)\n- **T3.4** Edit orchestration/SKILL.md row 6 + agents[] subsection (hook-based narrative supersedes manual-append) — overlaps with T1.1\n- **T3.5** Edit delegation/SKILL.md (structured-header convention codified per D-3-4)\n\nNote: T1.1 and T3.4 both touch orchestration/SKILL.md. Decide: merge into a single task touching both rows OR keep separate and serialize. Recommend: MERGE into T1.1 (single coherent edit to orchestration/SKILL.md covering row 5.5 + row 6 narrative + agents[] subsection).\n\nAfter merging, expect ~10 tasks total.\n\n### Sub-step C — Dependency Graph (When)\n\nBuild two tables:\n1. **Dependency table** — for each task, which other tasks must complete before it can start.\n2. **Parallel lane table** — group tasks that have no overlap (no shared files) into parallel lanes.\n\nReminder from Ideation D-3-5 + leader's iter3 cross-cutting observation: T1 doc edits must land BEFORE T3 hook + script, because T1 changes `cwd` semantics that T3 hook relies on.\n\nReminder from Preparation D-3 + edit-contract: tasks editing workspace skill files (.claude/skills/) must use the Edit tool (preserves inode); never `sed -i`. For bulk multi-file rewrites, edit canonical mirror path. T1 + T3 executor briefs must include this discipline.\n\nFlag any file-overlap conflicts between proposed parallel lanes.\n\n### Sub-step D — Agent Assignment (Who) + Required Skills\n\nFor each task:\n- Agent type (default: executor; leader for sub-planning; assistant for trivial)\n- Mandatory skills (Load Directives tier 3) per role × phase × file-touched\n- Mandatory mistakes (Load Directives tier 4) — per Preparation D-3, every T1 task brief MUST include:\n  - `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md`\n  - `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/manager-rm-rf-without-investigating-tracked-files.md`\n  - `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/manager-iter2-brief-failed-iron-law-7-verbatim-spec-recheck.md`\n  (procedural — Planning brief construction; relevant to manager more than executor, but cite anyway)\n- Plus per-task-specific mistakes (e.g., T3.1 hook script must ci